  "final_answer_text": "There are two sensor plugins that plausibly qualify for \"position tracking\" on the Otter:\n\n1. **`gps`** (domain: `ABSOLUTE_POSITIONING`) — direct absolute position fixes.\n2. **`ins-gps-fusion`** (domain: `DERIVED`) — a fused inertial+GPS position/attitude estimate, likely smoother and more complete (velocity/attitude too) but derived from GPS+IMU rather than a raw measurement.\n\nThere's also `imu` (`RELATIVE_POSITIONING`), but that only gives relative motion (accelerations/angular rates), not position tracking by itself — I wouldn't count it as a position sensor on its own.\n\n**My recommendation/default:** add both `gps` and `imu`, since `imu` is needed to feed `ins-gps-fusion` and raw `gps` is the simplest, most direct position-tracking sensor. However, since you specifically want \"position tracking,\" I'll default to just **`gps`** alone unless you want the fused estimate instead.\n\nPlease clarify which you'd prefer:\n- **(a)** `gps` only — simple, direct absolute position (default I'll use if you don't specify),\n- **(b)** `ins-gps-fusion` only — smoothed/derived position+attitude estimate (requires no extra sensor entry, but internally likely relies on GPS/IMU being enabled too — let me know if you want me to add `imu` alongside it),\n- **(c)** both `gps` and `ins-gps-fusion` for redundancy/comparison.\n\nIf you don't specify, I'll proceed with **option (a): `gps` only**, added to an Otter (`vehicle-a-otter`) scenario. Let me know your choice, or confirm the default, and provide any other scenario details (mission waypoints, duration, timestep, backend) so I can construct and validate the full scenario.",
